WEBVTT

00:01.251 --> 00:03.462
[waves crashing]

00:04.630 --> 00:07.132
[wind howling]

00:08.467 --> 00:10.219
[Sarah breathing heavily]

00:12.346 --> 00:13.805
[grunts]

00:20.270 --> 00:22.563
[breathing heavily]

00:22.564 --> 00:23.565
[grunts]

00:29.321 --> 00:30.405
Be not afraid.

00:31.448 --> 00:33.032
[Thomas] What's happening to me?

00:33.033 --> 00:35.035
[unsettling music playing]

00:40.040 --> 00:41.874
- [Holyoke] I can't see anything.
- Oh, God.

00:41.875 --> 00:44.293
[Thomas coughs]

00:44.294 --> 00:46.171
[Frances shrieks]

00:47.548 --> 00:51.592
- [breathing heavily]
- [Cromwell coughs]

00:51.593 --> 00:53.846
Frances. Frances!

00:54.930 --> 00:55.931
Frances!

00:57.140 --> 00:58.600
- Frances!
- [Frances inhales sharply]

01:01.061 --> 01:02.729
- Frances?
- [Frances] Help!

01:03.438 --> 01:04.772
- [Sarah] Frances!
- [Frances coughs]

01:05.440 --> 01:06.607
[Sarah] Frances!

01:06.608 --> 01:09.527
[coughing continues]

01:09.528 --> 01:11.070
[grunts]

01:11.071 --> 01:12.072
Grab hold!

01:15.701 --> 01:17.368
[Frances gasping]

01:17.369 --> 01:19.496
- [Sarah] Grab ahold.
- [Frances breathes heavily]

01:23.250 --> 01:25.334
[breathes heavily]

01:25.335 --> 01:28.255
[Sarah] Hold on. I'm-I'm trying, Frances!

01:29.298 --> 01:30.548
Don't let go!

01:30.549 --> 01:34.052
[Sarah coughs, speaks indistinctly]

01:47.357 --> 01:50.360
[unsettling music continues]

01:55.449 --> 01:57.284
[thunder crashes]

02:09.253 --> 02:11.256
[music fades]

02:12.341 --> 02:14.092
You have to sound the siren, Tom.

02:15.344 --> 02:16.553
[townsperson] She's right.

02:17.095 --> 02:19.014
Those thunderheads ain't natural.

02:19.681 --> 02:22.726
Read the accounts of the Storm of 1783.

02:23.310 --> 02:27.147
Started with big, ugly
storm clouds just like that.

02:28.190 --> 02:31.318
Storm roared in like The Great Flood.

02:31.985 --> 02:35.279
Storm brought waterspouts and tornadoes.

02:35.280 --> 02:38.199
Men were ripped up into the black sky.

02:38.200 --> 02:41.161
Babies torn from their mothers' arms.

02:43.121 --> 02:44.748
[electricity buzzing]

02:57.469 --> 03:00.681
- [exhales deeply]
- [line rings]

03:02.599 --> 03:03.600
How we looking?

03:04.309 --> 03:05.644
[person] You got your Doppler up?

03:06.436 --> 03:07.437
Yeah.

03:09.773 --> 03:11.650
[sighs] It doesn't look great.

03:13.151 --> 03:14.902
What's the mainland saying?

03:14.903 --> 03:17.906
We lost contact with the mainland
20 minutes ago.

03:20.200 --> 03:22.870
Okay. Well, then keep me updated.

03:30.043 --> 03:31.169
You have to sound the siren.

03:31.170 --> 03:33.172
You have to get everyone
into the shelters.

03:35.382 --> 03:37.134
Right now, it's just a storm.

03:39.595 --> 03:44.182
If I… If I sound the siren,
that's all they'll say when they get home.

03:44.183 --> 03:47.853
They went to Widow's Bay
and ended up in a fucking storm shelter.

03:48.437 --> 03:50.897
That doesn't happen
on Martha's Vineyard. [sighs]

03:50.898 --> 03:52.316
At least they'll get back home.

03:53.817 --> 03:55.152
People have died, Tom.

04:03.202 --> 04:04.203
[grunts]

04:06.747 --> 04:07.748
[huffs]

04:09.249 --> 04:10.250
[exhales deeply]

04:12.794 --> 04:14.046
[inhales deeply]

04:14.796 --> 04:16.130
[exhales deeply]

04:18.425 --> 04:20.719
[breathes heavily]

04:22.721 --> 04:23.722
[exhales deeply]

04:30.062 --> 04:32.272
[huffs]

04:33.607 --> 04:36.067
- [huffs] Fuck.
- [Patricia] Oh, uh…

04:36.068 --> 04:37.194
Um…

04:37.945 --> 04:39.863
Shit. Shit. Shit.

04:40.364 --> 04:41.447
[huffs]

04:41.448 --> 04:43.075
[grunts] Fuck. [grunts]

04:43.825 --> 04:46.702
- [grunting]
- [Patricia] Uh… Tom!

04:46.703 --> 04:48.455
- [Tom huffs]
- Oh, my God.

04:50.415 --> 04:51.499
- You okay?
- No.

04:51.500 --> 04:53.710
My back. [straining] Can't move it.

04:54.545 --> 04:55.711
She's missing a finger.

04:55.712 --> 04:56.755
[straining] What?

04:57.798 --> 05:01.008
[wheezing] No, Patricia.
Patricia. Patricia.

05:01.009 --> 05:02.302
Patricia.

05:03.554 --> 05:06.013
- Oh, Kenny.
- [Rosemary] Everybody stay back.

05:06.014 --> 05:08.766
- [Tom] Oh, fuck. [grunts, groans]
- [Rosemary] Tom, what happened?

05:08.767 --> 05:11.477
- [Tom] Kenny.
- I said to stay back.

05:11.478 --> 05:14.022
- He might have broke something.
- [Tom] No. Let him help me.

05:14.565 --> 05:16.899
- Maybe if we both grab a side, we can--
- Back off, Kenny.

05:16.900 --> 05:19.068
He might have spinal damage.
Can't move him.

05:19.069 --> 05:21.279
I'll do it myself. Here we go.

05:21.280 --> 05:23.489
- No. No. [groans, grunts]
- [Rosemary] All right.

05:23.490 --> 05:25.700
You're pushing it down on me.
You're pushing it down on me.

05:25.701 --> 05:27.326
Don't speak, Tom.

05:27.327 --> 05:30.162
Your lungs might be collapsed.
All right, here we go. Ready?

05:30.163 --> 05:32.331
One, two, three.

05:32.332 --> 05:33.833
- Ow! Oh, my sciatica.
- [Tom grunts]

05:33.834 --> 05:35.376
- Oh. Poor Rosemary.
- [Rosemary] Shit.

05:35.377 --> 05:38.213
- [Dale] Oh, no.
- What? [coughing]

05:39.965 --> 05:42.509
[grunts, exhales deeply]

05:43.427 --> 05:44.970
Thanks, Kenny. [grunts]

05:45.971 --> 05:47.472
[Patricia] Tom, her finger.

05:48.056 --> 05:50.558
Look, Tom. It's missing.

05:50.559 --> 05:51.934
[Tom] What? [grunts]

05:51.935 --> 05:53.103
Frances Warren.

05:53.645 --> 05:56.356
Her brother ran over her ring finger.
It's in Sarah Warren's journal.

05:56.940 --> 05:57.941
[grunts]

05:59.401 --> 06:02.236
This woman in the painting,
Frances Fisher,

06:02.237 --> 06:04.406
mysteriously washed up on shore as a girl.

06:05.032 --> 06:07.116
This is Frances Warren.

06:07.117 --> 06:10.037
That's why Richard Warren's
bloodline didn't end with him.

06:10.746 --> 06:12.289
Because his daughter lived.

06:12.789 --> 06:14.666
[thunder crashes]

06:17.586 --> 06:18.587
[exhales deeply]

06:20.756 --> 06:21.757
Tom?

06:24.301 --> 06:25.302
[exhales deeply]

06:29.264 --> 06:30.265
[grunts]

06:34.436 --> 06:36.396
Tom, are you listening to me?

06:41.235 --> 06:42.236
[grunts]

06:44.029 --> 06:45.197
[clicks tongue]

06:46.365 --> 06:49.659
If that is Frances Warren,

06:49.660 --> 06:53.413
that's over 400 years
of ancestry to untangle.

06:54.248 --> 06:57.125
Rosemary probably
already has genealogy on Barnabus.

07:00.838 --> 07:03.048
And then what? We round them up?

07:08.720 --> 07:09.847
[breathes heavily]

07:11.348 --> 07:13.600
[exhales deeply]

07:21.233 --> 07:23.819
- [line rings]
- [sighs]

07:25.696 --> 07:27.239
[clicks tongue] This is Loftis.

07:29.867 --> 07:30.909
Hit the siren.

07:32.703 --> 07:35.121
[thunder rumbling]

07:35.122 --> 07:36.790
- [wind howling]
- [thunder rumbles]

07:53.307 --> 07:57.769
This ferry isn't coming,
and I wouldn't even get on it if it did.

07:58.979 --> 08:00.313
Can we please just go back home?

08:00.314 --> 08:03.859
No, listen, ferries operate
in storms all the time.

08:05.485 --> 08:08.197
[siren blaring]

08:14.620 --> 08:15.621
Bechir,

08:16.747 --> 08:17.872
get me home.

08:17.873 --> 08:20.124
[siren continues]

08:20.125 --> 08:21.710
I just need to try one more thing.

08:22.377 --> 08:23.378
All right? Okay.

08:29.343 --> 08:30.426
Stop…

08:30.427 --> 08:32.429
[speaking indistinctly]

08:58.455 --> 09:00.707
[Wyck] So, what's the plan here?

09:01.208 --> 09:02.835
I'm getting the fuck off this island.

09:03.752 --> 09:05.170
I know how to operate a boat.

09:06.171 --> 09:07.798
Forty miles from the mainland.

09:08.465 --> 09:11.969
In a boat with a range of 15 miles tops
with a full tank.

09:12.970 --> 09:16.639
And even if you do somehow refuel

09:16.640 --> 09:20.644
while in the middle of this storm,
the waves'll capsize you.

09:21.770 --> 09:23.313
I can't have my child here.

09:25.983 --> 09:27.150
I understand that, but…

09:27.985 --> 09:30.319
That boat came here on a boat.

09:30.320 --> 09:32.614
Not gonna get you to the mainland in this.

09:49.798 --> 09:50.883
[grunts]

10:00.058 --> 10:01.476
What have you told her?

10:05.397 --> 10:06.398
Nothing.

10:08.192 --> 10:09.610
I can't tell her anything.

10:11.153 --> 10:14.323
- [dramatic music playing]
- [siren continues]

10:14.907 --> 10:17.618
[automated voice] Attention residents
and visitors to Widow's Bay.

10:18.202 --> 10:22.121
There is a mandatory storm advisory
by order of the mayor.

10:22.122 --> 10:24.666
Report to the shelter immediately.

10:25.584 --> 10:28.337
Attention residents
and visitors to Widow's Bay…

10:57.783 --> 11:00.077
[dramatic music continues]

11:07.209 --> 11:09.211
[people chattering]

11:12.798 --> 11:13.881
[person] Sorry.

11:13.882 --> 11:16.050
[Tom] All right everyone,
head towards my voice.

11:16.051 --> 11:18.804
Make this left. Make your way downstairs.

11:19.346 --> 11:22.056
Welcome to your first nor'easter, folks.

11:22.057 --> 11:26.353
After this, you're gonna be one of us.
A real New Englander.

11:26.979 --> 11:30.690
Heard it's, uh… Heard it's hitting
Martha's Vineyard pretty hard.

11:30.691 --> 11:33.861
Now you'll be refunded
by your accommodations for tonight.

11:34.736 --> 11:35.946
That money's already spent.

11:36.530 --> 11:38.073
- Okay.
- [music fades]

11:40.868 --> 11:41.869
[mouthing] Come here.

11:45.622 --> 11:48.791
I know, I know. I just… I had to make sure
PJ and those guys were all coming.

11:48.792 --> 11:51.711
Listen, I know we do this dance a lot.

11:51.712 --> 11:52.920
Today, please--

11:52.921 --> 11:54.755
- I'm not gonna go anywhere.
- Can you-- Okay.

11:54.756 --> 11:56.048
- I promise.
- Okay, good.

11:56.049 --> 11:59.677
And hey, we can go
to a Sox game whenever, you know.

11:59.678 --> 12:01.847
I mean, they still have
half a season left, so…

12:05.100 --> 12:06.559
I love you, bud.

12:06.560 --> 12:08.019
All right, go downstairs.

12:08.020 --> 12:09.021
Okay.

12:11.148 --> 12:12.608
We have an issue.

12:13.525 --> 12:14.943
[Kenny] Generator's out.

12:15.652 --> 12:19.197
The emergency lights run on batteries.
They'll last a half hour,

12:19.198 --> 12:21.157
then the shelter goes pitch-black.

12:21.158 --> 12:22.700
Oh, my God.

12:22.701 --> 12:24.660
There's power surges
through the whole island.

12:24.661 --> 12:27.038
'Cause of the storm,
it's overloading the grid.

12:27.039 --> 12:29.248
Even the heavy-duty gear is getting fried.

12:29.249 --> 12:32.126
So-So what do we do?
We have to get power down there.

12:32.127 --> 12:33.794
Garrett might have a replacement.

12:33.795 --> 12:35.797
He's got the same one
up at the lighthouse.

12:37.716 --> 12:39.301
- [radio beeps]
- [Tom] Garrett.

12:41.762 --> 12:44.138
Garrett, I'm looking right now.
I don't see you…

12:44.139 --> 12:45.973
Oh, oh. All right, listen. Listen to me.

12:45.974 --> 12:49.060
We need your starter
for the old generator.

12:49.061 --> 12:51.521
[Garret, distorted] I can't understand
a goddamn word you're saying.

12:51.522 --> 12:52.855
- Do--
- [feedback on radio]

12:52.856 --> 12:54.357
Does he not have a goddamn phone?

12:54.358 --> 12:56.235
- No.
- [static crackles]

12:57.653 --> 12:58.736
Garrett.

12:58.737 --> 13:01.656
[Garret, distorted] How the hell am I
supposed to get you a goddamn starter?

13:01.657 --> 13:04.075
- Garrett, Garrett. I can't hear…
- [static crackling]

13:04.076 --> 13:06.911
We need your starter.

13:06.912 --> 13:08.621
- This is an emergency.
- [feedback whining]

13:08.622 --> 13:11.123
- I'm going up there.
- Tom, you shouldn't go out there.

13:11.124 --> 13:12.416
It's not safe.

13:12.417 --> 13:13.836
[thunder rumbles]

13:30.894 --> 13:33.105
[thunderclap]

13:34.106 --> 13:35.691
[pants]

13:36.608 --> 13:37.943
[Bechir] Let's get you warm.

13:38.443 --> 13:40.319
- [door closes]
- Let me help you.

13:40.320 --> 13:41.363
- Okay.
- [Chelle groans]

13:42.865 --> 13:44.073
What's wrong, hon?

13:44.074 --> 13:46.618
Uh, maybe it's just Braxton Hicks.

13:48.412 --> 13:49.871
Dr. Morgan's downstairs.

13:49.872 --> 13:51.415
- Let's get you comfortable.
- Okay.

13:52.457 --> 13:53.458
[Chelle groans]

14:01.758 --> 14:02.842
[sighs]

14:02.843 --> 14:05.512
[eerie music playing]

14:31.038 --> 14:32.456
[music fades]

14:36.585 --> 14:37.628
[sighs]

14:38.462 --> 14:39.880
[gasps, sighs]

14:40.464 --> 14:42.673
You need to learn to knock, cowboy.

14:42.674 --> 14:44.968
This is a castle doctrine town.

14:45.469 --> 14:48.554
Funny to think the whole island survived

14:48.555 --> 14:51.391
on whale blubber
well into my father's day.

14:52.059 --> 14:54.269
The whaler, the captain, they…

14:54.978 --> 14:57.564
they owned this place, my daddy would say.

14:58.232 --> 15:00.067
[sighs] What's this about, Wyck?

15:05.155 --> 15:06.490
[sighs]

15:16.834 --> 15:18.835
I need you to do something for me.

15:18.836 --> 15:20.838
[dramatic music playing]

15:27.094 --> 15:29.763
[thunder rumbling]

15:36.895 --> 15:39.898
[radio crackling]

15:41.066 --> 15:43.569
[distorted music playing]

15:46.029 --> 15:47.780
[radio crackling]

15:47.781 --> 15:49.783
[distorted music playing]

15:54.162 --> 15:56.122
- [crackling continues]
- [hits dash]

15:56.123 --> 15:57.624
[distorted music stops]

16:00.460 --> 16:02.462
[dramatic music continues]

16:15.893 --> 16:18.312
[chains clinking]

16:31.241 --> 16:32.326
Garrett!

16:36.663 --> 16:37.748
Garrett!

16:40.083 --> 16:41.126
Fuck!

16:47.216 --> 16:49.384
No. No!

16:51.762 --> 16:52.763
Shit.

17:03.357 --> 17:04.358
[Tom] Garrett?

17:06.818 --> 17:09.445
Goddamn it, Garrett,
I came here for the starter.

17:12.532 --> 17:14.534
Oh! Oh, thank God!

17:14.535 --> 17:16.452
- [Garret] I'll bring it back.
- What? No, no, no!

17:16.453 --> 17:18.453
No, stay there, stay there!
I'm coming to you!

17:18.454 --> 17:21.164
[stammers] I'm coming back!
I'm coming back!

17:21.165 --> 17:22.751
Dale, stop him!

17:25.337 --> 17:26.839
[thunder rumbles]

17:32.177 --> 17:34.179
[wind howling]

17:41.478 --> 17:43.480
[music intensifies]

17:45.941 --> 17:47.066
Fuck. No!

17:47.067 --> 17:50.028
[stammers] No, no! Garrett!

17:50.529 --> 17:52.196
- No.
- [blares horn]

17:52.197 --> 17:53.990
Garrett, go!

17:53.991 --> 17:56.660
Go, go, go, go, go!

17:57.202 --> 17:59.579
Get inside! Get inside!

17:59.580 --> 18:01.956
- [Todd] Hey, Wyck! Hey, hey, Wyck!
- [music fades]

18:01.957 --> 18:03.959
- Shaman?
- Wyck!

18:04.459 --> 18:05.835
[Tom] Come inside!

18:05.836 --> 18:08.004
- Help me out!
- No, no, no! Come inside!

18:08.005 --> 18:10.131
- No, no, come on!
- [Todd groans]

18:10.132 --> 18:11.340
Help me, man!

18:11.341 --> 18:12.967
No, no! Leave it, leave it!

18:12.968 --> 18:15.636
- I need these!
- Come inside!

18:15.637 --> 18:18.848
[storm rumbles, howls]

18:18.849 --> 18:20.767
Come inside! Come inside right now!

18:21.643 --> 18:23.186
[Todd] Wyck!

18:23.187 --> 18:25.189
[screaming]

18:28.942 --> 18:30.944
[dramatic music playing]

18:38.035 --> 18:39.203
[music stops]

19:00.307 --> 19:01.807
No one leaves this shelter.

19:01.808 --> 19:03.809
Do you understand? No matter what happens.

19:03.810 --> 19:06.062
Ruth's not here.

19:06.063 --> 19:07.396
She's home.

19:07.397 --> 19:08.481
Alone.

19:08.482 --> 19:11.526
Okay, all right,
I'll-I'll-I'll figure something out.

19:11.527 --> 19:13.444
We won't leave her out there.

19:13.445 --> 19:15.989
- [thunder rumbles]
- [lights clinking]

19:20.994 --> 19:21.995
[Wyck] Loftis.

19:27.292 --> 19:29.211
There's something you both should see.

19:40.889 --> 19:42.099
[Tom] What is this?

19:43.141 --> 19:44.852
I had her run a genealogy.

19:46.520 --> 19:49.355
You-You-You can't be serious.
Th-This-This is…

19:49.356 --> 19:51.399
- Wyck, we don't have time for that.
- I had to know.

19:51.400 --> 19:53.192
Know what, Wyck?

19:53.193 --> 19:58.282
Turned out Richard Warren
has one last living descendant.

20:01.243 --> 20:02.244
One?

20:02.995 --> 20:04.078
Who is it?

20:04.079 --> 20:06.831
No. Don't answer that.
It doesn't matter who it is.

20:06.832 --> 20:09.042
- We're not--
- Who is it?

20:09.751 --> 20:11.502
- Have a seat.
- Goddamn it, Rosemary!

20:11.503 --> 20:13.380
We don't have time for this.
Tell me who it is.

20:24.600 --> 20:25.601
[sighs]

20:26.602 --> 20:28.812
Tom, you're not really
gonna listen to this.

20:41.366 --> 20:43.075
[Rosemary sighs]

20:43.076 --> 20:44.453
All right. Here we go.

20:46.622 --> 20:51.083
Warren and the first wife, Sybil,
lost their first two boys

20:51.084 --> 20:53.170
when they reached the island.

20:53.670 --> 20:57.965
As for the others,
didn't work out so well for them either.

20:57.966 --> 21:01.594
Nope. Tough break. Sorry, kid.

21:01.595 --> 21:03.596
Better luck next time. [sighs]

21:03.597 --> 21:05.933
Okay, I want you to picture this.

21:06.600 --> 21:10.561
You're a little girl, and your finger
gets broken off by a wagon wheel.

21:10.562 --> 21:13.064
Next thing you know, your dad's dead,

21:13.065 --> 21:15.942
and your stepmom
is taking you on an adventure.

21:15.943 --> 21:17.736
Destination? Hell.

21:18.403 --> 21:19.530
Your name?

21:20.113 --> 21:23.116
Frances Warren.

21:23.867 --> 21:25.618
Now, your siblings are dead,

21:25.619 --> 21:27.870
but God's finger flicks you
on the back of the head,

21:27.871 --> 21:29.497
and you float back to shore.

21:29.498 --> 21:33.125
Lucky you, Barnabus Fisher finds you
on his way back from a whaling trip,

21:33.126 --> 21:35.378
takes pity on you, little girl.

21:35.379 --> 21:38.130
Feeds you, clothes you, raises you.

21:38.131 --> 21:39.550
Wealthy man.

21:40.551 --> 21:42.261
It must be nice.

21:46.139 --> 21:49.685
- [coughing]
- [Rosemary sighs] All right. Where was I?

21:50.644 --> 21:54.689
Fast forward a few years
and you're in the bloom of youth.

21:54.690 --> 21:56.983
- [fan whirring]
- [sighs] No, I can't hear.

21:56.984 --> 21:58.902
I… I can't hear.

22:00.320 --> 22:01.946
[whirring stops]

22:01.947 --> 22:05.284
Okay. You're 14 years old.

22:05.951 --> 22:08.078
Barnabus starts
to look at you differently.

22:08.787 --> 22:11.539
He sits you down
over a cup of whale fin soup

22:11.540 --> 22:14.375
and he tells you
things are gonna be different.

22:14.376 --> 22:18.421
He's ripping pages off the calendar.
X. X. X. He's counting down.

22:18.422 --> 22:21.257
Get you a white dress,
takes you to the pastor who says,

22:21.258 --> 22:23.217
"All right, I guess."
And now you're married.

22:23.218 --> 22:25.178
You suffer a few miserable years.

22:25.179 --> 22:29.266
Barnabus drops dead,
leaving you his whaling business

22:30.642 --> 22:32.019
and also a son.

22:32.686 --> 22:35.563
Jonathan is a healthy baby boy,

22:35.564 --> 22:38.984
and when he grows up,
he won't be shooting blanks.

22:39.902 --> 22:41.403
He is a stud.

22:42.237 --> 22:46.699
Now, here is where we reach
a few ends that are dead.

22:46.700 --> 22:49.995
Dead baby. Dead baby. Lesbian.

22:50.537 --> 22:53.582
Sophia "The Heretic"
marries Byron Fairclough.

22:54.291 --> 22:57.668
These jackrabbits had six kids,

22:57.669 --> 23:00.630
and some of them have a few of their own,

23:00.631 --> 23:01.964
but you know what they say,

23:01.965 --> 23:04.800
"A family that swims together,
drowns together."

23:04.801 --> 23:07.970
And so, the inaugural swim is born.

23:07.971 --> 23:09.556
That's not a saying.

23:10.974 --> 23:13.142
Well, I guess I don't know
what I'm talking about

23:13.143 --> 23:14.770
and should just stop.

23:17.856 --> 23:19.775
- [Tom clicks tongue]
- [Rosemary exhales deeply]

23:20.400 --> 23:22.361
I'm sorry. Please go on.

23:27.824 --> 23:29.159
[Rosemary clears throat]

23:30.202 --> 23:33.205
[Rosemary] Oh. No good news here.

23:33.747 --> 23:36.874
Dead baby. Dead baby. Lesbian.

23:36.875 --> 23:38.334
Can you please stop saying lesbian?

23:38.335 --> 23:40.127
I can't say that now?

23:40.128 --> 23:41.963
It's the way you're saying it.

23:41.964 --> 23:43.465
[Rosemary] Ugh. Fine.

23:43.966 --> 23:48.177
- Anyway, this next batch, all retards--
- Rosemary!

23:48.178 --> 23:50.847
- [Wyck sighs]
- Can you please just get on with it?

23:50.848 --> 23:51.974
Please.

23:53.392 --> 23:57.353
[Rosemary]
Joseph "The Faithful" has three kids.

23:57.354 --> 24:00.982
Rumor is, two of the siblings
took up with each other,

24:00.983 --> 24:03.609
which is their business
as far as I'm concerned,

24:03.610 --> 24:05.237
unless they have children.

24:06.405 --> 24:07.989
And in this case, they did.

24:07.990 --> 24:09.783
You can imagine how that went.

24:10.450 --> 24:13.703
Elizabeth spits out several kids.

24:13.704 --> 24:16.038
Jeremiah, Abigail, and Madorah.

24:16.039 --> 24:17.666
They're all tickets to nowhere.

24:18.417 --> 24:21.211
Oh, I could tell you their story
if-if we're not in a rush.

24:22.212 --> 24:23.297
[Wyck] Hmm.

24:25.465 --> 24:27.633
I suppose we're in a rush.

24:27.634 --> 24:31.679
Elizabeth's daughter, Grace,
marries Abraham Fitzgerald,

24:31.680 --> 24:34.933
and they have two daughters.
"The Ungrateful Hortence"…

24:35.601 --> 24:37.435
Things didn't turn out so well for her…

24:37.436 --> 24:39.645
and Anne Fitzgerald.

24:39.646 --> 24:41.397
She wasn't much to look at either,

24:41.398 --> 24:44.651
but she played her cards right, you know,
and married Hezekiah.

24:46.028 --> 24:51.073
Her son gives birth to Mabel,
who marries Luther Sullivan.

24:51.074 --> 24:54.203
And we have dead baby.

24:54.703 --> 24:58.372
And a daughter with
a bunch of kids who died.

24:58.373 --> 25:00.834
[chuckles] It's a great murder mystery.

25:01.877 --> 25:04.922
But I'll get on with it,
like Tom wants. [sighs]

25:05.881 --> 25:07.757
[whispers] It was the husband.

25:07.758 --> 25:09.842
- [projector sheets rustle]
- [normal] Henry.

25:09.843 --> 25:12.345
Henry does okay and gives birth to Ida.

25:12.346 --> 25:16.140
Ida and Frederick Long
give birth to Clarabell.

25:16.141 --> 25:17.433
I've seen her portrait.

25:17.434 --> 25:19.435
She thinks she's something.

25:19.436 --> 25:22.605
Clarabell marries Benjamin
and gives birth to Edward,

25:22.606 --> 25:23.649
and he's not much.

25:24.441 --> 25:26.360
And now we're in the 1900s, people.

25:27.694 --> 25:28.986
We get two brothers.

25:28.987 --> 25:31.697
Grant Livingston,
who tried to build a submarine,

25:31.698 --> 25:33.242
you can guess how that ended,

25:33.742 --> 25:38.162
and Charles Livingston marries Florence,

25:38.163 --> 25:43.377
which brings me to the final
living descendant of Richard Warren.

25:44.545 --> 25:47.630
[thunderclap, rumbling]

25:47.631 --> 25:51.385
And to my knowledge,
has no clue about their lineage.

25:52.010 --> 25:54.804
Never married, never had children,

25:54.805 --> 26:00.269
which is surprising
because this one was a real beaut.

26:05.816 --> 26:08.610
Miss Widow's Bay, 1959.

26:14.199 --> 26:15.284
So, there's just one?

26:16.827 --> 26:20.413
One-One descendant of Warren
that's still alive?

26:20.414 --> 26:22.082
Just one in the bloodline, and…

26:23.292 --> 26:24.543
and they're old?

26:29.965 --> 26:31.633
[sighs]

26:45.939 --> 26:47.815
What do we know about her health?

26:47.816 --> 26:50.151
- [Patricia] Why are you even asking that?
- You know why.

26:50.152 --> 26:51.403
I hope to hell not.

26:52.029 --> 26:54.406
I mean, how much time
does she even have left?

26:55.282 --> 26:57.201
I can't believe this.

26:58.368 --> 27:00.913
This is a woman
who bakes us birthday cakes.

27:02.206 --> 27:04.040
Who lets your son stay in her home.

27:04.041 --> 27:05.125
Patricia…

27:06.043 --> 27:07.085
[sighs]

27:07.711 --> 27:09.254
…no one wants this.

27:10.339 --> 27:14.343
But there are hundreds of lives at stake,
and one of them is my son.

27:15.427 --> 27:16.929
And that justifies murder?

27:17.554 --> 27:19.555
You can sit there and say all you want,

27:19.556 --> 27:22.099
but you don't know what
the fuck I just saw out there.

27:22.100 --> 27:23.184
This is f…

27:23.185 --> 27:24.186
[chuckles]

27:25.687 --> 27:27.021
This is fucking bad.

27:27.022 --> 27:28.856
If it's done, it needs to be quick.

27:28.857 --> 27:30.525
A gunshot, back of the head.

27:30.526 --> 27:31.776
Oh, my God.

27:31.777 --> 27:34.028
- [Tom] All right, Wyck, come on.
- It's barbaric.

27:34.029 --> 27:36.490
It's the kind thing to do.
She wouldn't see it coming.

27:39.535 --> 27:40.911
[Patricia] Do you hear him?

27:42.287 --> 27:43.997
You're actually considering this?

27:45.624 --> 27:47.084
What would that make you?

27:49.044 --> 27:50.295
What's it say about us?

27:51.421 --> 27:52.505
About this place?

27:52.506 --> 27:55.132
You want Evan to grow up
in a place that does something like that?

27:55.133 --> 27:57.218
He wouldn't have to grow up
in this place at all.

27:57.219 --> 27:58.637
He shouldn't have to.

27:59.388 --> 28:00.973
When she dies, it ends.

28:02.099 --> 28:03.392
She lived a good life.

28:04.309 --> 28:06.436
So, what if she's old? You're old.

28:07.020 --> 28:09.313
Would you want to be killed if it was you
just 'cause you're old?

28:09.314 --> 28:11.525
I was willing to put the gun
in my mouth myself.

28:12.234 --> 28:14.069
- Look, she's not married.
- [Patricia] So?

28:14.695 --> 28:17.446
- I wasn't finished.
- Oh, cool. Keep going then.

28:17.447 --> 28:19.032
She also never had children.

28:20.826 --> 28:22.702
- Well…
- [phone rings]

28:22.703 --> 28:26.205
Thank God I'm not a descendant, or I guess
my throat would already be slit.

28:26.206 --> 28:28.083
This isn't about you.

28:30.419 --> 28:32.087
[ringing continues, stops]

28:32.713 --> 28:35.047
- [static crackling]
- [person speaks indistinctly]

28:35.048 --> 28:36.175
Mitch?

28:36.800 --> 28:38.718
[Mitch, distorted] Oh, God. It's going.

28:38.719 --> 28:41.179
- What-What's going?
- It's all going!

28:41.180 --> 28:43.556
- Mitch, what-what's going?
- [line disconnects]

28:43.557 --> 28:44.766
Mitch? Mitch?

28:46.768 --> 28:47.852
What is it?

28:47.853 --> 28:50.938
I'm not trying to say I told you so,
but you brought families here.

28:50.939 --> 28:53.609
It's been 300 years of hell on this place!

28:54.318 --> 28:55.651
It needs to end.

28:55.652 --> 28:56.986
Don't try to drag it out.

28:56.987 --> 28:59.698
I can make it quick. Peaceful.

29:01.408 --> 29:03.035
You're not doing anything.

29:04.244 --> 29:05.495
What does that mean?

29:07.122 --> 29:08.456
What are you gonna do?

29:08.457 --> 29:10.792
[tense music playing]

29:17.132 --> 29:19.551
[thunderclap, rumbling]
